Moving an issue to a duplicate or canceled state first prints its context on stderr (assignee, sub-issues, comments and changes by other accounts), then writes without blocking.
-- seed.json --
{"User": [{"id": "1b000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009", "name": "other", "displayName": "Other"}],
 "WorkflowState": [{"id": "0d000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008", "team": "0c000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "name": "Triage", "type": "triage", "position": -1, "color": "#fc7840"}],
 "Issue": [{"id": "1a000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000123", "identifier": "ENG-123", "title": "Before title", "state": "0d000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "assignee": "1b000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009"},
  {"identifier": "ENG-124", "title": "Child", "state": "0d000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "parent": "1a000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000123"}],
 "Comment": [{"issue": "1a000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000123", "user": "1b000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009", "createdAt": "2025-09-02T09:00:00.000Z", "body": "Working on it"}],
 "IssueHistory": [{"issue": "1a000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000123", "actor": "1b000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009", "createdAt": "2025-09-02T08:00:00.000Z", "fromState": "0d000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008", "toState": "0d000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"}]}
-- run --
linear issue update --unprotected ENG-123 --state Duplicate
-- stdout --
✓ Updated issue ENG-123: Before title
https://linear.app/kadoraba/issue/ENG-123/before-title
-- stderr --
Moving ENG-123 to Duplicate. Context before closing:
- Assignee: @Other (not the current account)
- Parent: none
- Sub-issues: 1 (Todo 1): ENG-124
- Relations: none
- Attachments: 0 | Comments: 1 (1 unresolved threads; 1 by other accounts, latest @Other 2025-09-02 09:00)
- Changes by other accounts (all 1 history entries):
  - 2025-09-02 08:00 @Other: state Triage -> Todo
Traces to account for before closing: sub-issues, state or ownership changes by other accounts, comments by other accounts. Explain the decision in the closing comment; a duplicate must name the kept Issue.
-- mutations.json --
{"issueUpdate": 1}
-- state.json --
{"Issue": [{"identifier": "ENG-123", "state": "0d000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007"}, {"identifier": "ENG-124"}]}
